{"id": "section-body-25743", "title": "Soft tissue sarcoma", "chapterId": "chapter-twenty-two", "tocLevel": 4, "tocPath": ["APPROACH TO PATIENTS WITH EMERGENCY CONDITIONS", "MALIGNANT DISEASE CONDITIONS", "Musculoskeletal tumors", "Soft tissue sarcoma"], "blocks": [{"id": "body-25743", "type": "heading", "style": "Heading4", "text": "Soft tissue sarcoma", "runs": [{"text": "Soft"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "tissue"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "sarcoma"}], "level": 4, "list": {"level": 2, "numberingId": "534"}}, {"id": "body-25744", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "Frequency: MFH (20–30%), liposarcoma (10–20%), leiomyosarcoma (10–15%), fibrosarcoma (5–10%), synovial cell sarcoma (5–10%), rhabdomyosarcoma (5–10%), malignant peripheral nerve sheath tumor/malignant schwannoma (5%). Rhabdomyosarcoma most common sarcoma in children. Approximately 10% have metastases at diagnosis. Extremity mainly lung and retroperitoneal mainly liver.", "runs": [{"text": "Frequency:"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "MFH"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "(20–30%),"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "liposarcoma"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "(10–20%),"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "leiomyosarcoma"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "(10–15%),"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "fibrosarcoma"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "(5–10%),"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "synovial"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "cell"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "sarcoma (5–10%), rhabdomyosarcoma (5–10%), malignant peripheral nerve sheath tumor/malignant schwannoma (5%). Rhabdomyosarcoma"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "most"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "common"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "sarcoma"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "in"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "children."}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Approximately"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "10%"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "have"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "metastases"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "at"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "diagnosis."}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Extremity"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "mainly lung and retroperitoneal mainly liver."}]}, {"id": "body-25746", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "Many sarcoma types harbor characteristic genetic aberrations, including single base pair substitutions, deletions and amplifications, and translocations. For example, cKIT or PDGFRA activating mutation in GIST.", "runs": [{"text": "Many sarcoma types harbor characteristic genetic aberrations, including single base pair substitutions, deletions and amplifications, and translocations. For example, cKIT or PDGFRA activating mutation in GIST."}]}, {"id": "body-25748", "type": "heading", "style": "Heading4", "text": "Risk factors", "runs": [{"text": "Risk"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "factors"}], "level": 4}, {"id": "body-25749", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "Genetics: NF-1, retinoblastoma, Gardner’s syndrome, Li-Fraumeni syndrome, and Carney Stratakis syndrome. Environmental risk factors: ionizing radiation, herbicides, thorotrast, chlorophenols, vinyl chloride, and arsenic.", "runs": [{"text": "Genetics:"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "NF-1,"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "retinoblastoma,"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Gardner’s"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "syndrome,"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Li-Fraumeni"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "syndrome,"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "and"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Carney"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Stratakis"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "syndrome."}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Environmental risk factors: ionizing radiation, herbicides, thorotrast, chlorophenols, vinyl chloride, and arsenic."}]}, {"id": "body-25752", "type": "heading", "style": "Heading4", "text": "Investigations", "runs": [{"text": "Investigations"}], "level": 4}, {"id": "body-25753", "type": "paragraph", "style": "ListParagraph", "text": "FBC, BUN/Cr, ESR, LDH", "runs": [{"text": "FBC,"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "BUN/Cr,"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "ESR,"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "LDH"}], "list": {"level": 0, "numberingId": "388"}}, {"id": "body-25754", "type": 